IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `hcsc-dates`
IMPORT `hcsc-core`
IMPORT `hcsc-seat`

-- Health and Community Services Complaints Act 2004 (SA) -- cases for the seat of the person complaining
-- (hcsc-seat.l4). Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text (the section is named on each group),
-- never copied from the encoding's output; day counts are shown where they matter. Edges: 2 years to the day, and the
-- day after; 29 February plus 2 years; the s 27(3) presumption both ways; 31 May and 1 June 2004 (s 27(2)(b)); the 45th
-- and 46th day (s 29(1)), with and without allowed delay, across a year end; the 14th and 15th day (ss 29(6), 42(2)),
-- across a leap February; the child's 16th birthday (s 24(b)); each "means" exclusion; each s 25(2), (4) carve-out.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases: the person complaining`

-- Any date, for an input the question does not read.
`ANY` MEANS `the date` 1 1 2000

§§ `s 4 and reg 4 -- is it a health or community service`

#ASSERT `Is my service one I can complain about` `an ambulance service` FALSE EQUALS `yes: it is a health service, s 4 definition of health service, paragraph` "(d)"
#ASSERT `Is my service one I can complain about` `a service provided by a health professional` FALSE EQUALS `yes: it is a health service, s 4 definition of health service, paragraph` "(f)"
#ASSERT `Is my service one I can complain about` `a service designed to benefit or promote human health` FALSE EQUALS `yes: it is a health service, s 4 definition of health service, paragraph` "(a)"
#ASSERT `Is my service one I can complain about` `a social, welfare, recreational or leisure service provided as part of a health service` FALSE EQUALS `yes: it is a health service, s 4 definition of health service, paragraph` "(i)"
#ASSERT `Is my service one I can complain about` `a service for the care or protection of a child at risk` FALSE EQUALS `yes: it is a community service, s 4 definition of community service, paragraph` "(c)"
#ASSERT `Is my service one I can complain about` `an administration service directly related to a community service` FALSE EQUALS `yes: it is a community service, s 4 definition of community service, paragraph` "(f)"
-- An independent medical report for an insurer is a health status report: excluded by s 4 health service (k).
#ASSERT `Is my service one I can complain about` `the writing or content of a health status report` FALSE EQUALS `no: the definition of health service does not include the process of writing, or the content of, a health status report (a report on a person's health prepared for a purpose other than providing a health service) (s 4, health service (k))`
#ASSERT `Is my service one I can complain about` `an employment search or placement service, or employment related training or retraining` FALSE EQUALS `no: the definition of community service does not include employment search or placement services, or employment related training or retraining (s 4, community service (g))`
-- reg 4: excluded only where Tribunal review is open; otherwise community service (a) (fork F2).
#ASSERT `Is my service one I can complain about` `a housing service of the South Australian Housing Trust or a registered community housing provider` TRUE EQUALS `no: a housing service of the South Australian Housing Trust or a registered community housing provider is excluded where you can have its decision reviewed by the South Australian Civil and Administrative Tribunal (reg 4)`
#ASSERT `Is my service one I can complain about` `a housing service of the South Australian Housing Trust or a registered community housing provider` FALSE EQUALS `yes: it is a community service, s 4 definition of community service, paragraph` "(a)"
#ASSERT `Is my service one I can complain about` `none of these` FALSE EQUALS `no: it is not within the definition of health service or of community service (s 4; both are "means" definitions)`

§§ `s 24 -- who may complain`

`ONLYIF` MEANS `only if the Commissioner approves you to act for the consumer, being satisfied that it is unreasonable to expect the consumer to complain personally (s 24(g)), or is of the opinion that you should be able to make this complaint in the public interest (s 24(l))`

#ASSERT `May I make this complaint` `the consumer` 40 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: you may make the complaint under` "s 24(a)"
#ASSERT `May I make this complaint` `the consumer` 10 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: you may make the complaint under` "s 24(a) and (b)(i)"
-- the 16th birthday: (b)(ii) from 16, (b)(iii) below 16.
#ASSERT `May I make this complaint` `a person the consumer appointed to complain for them` 16 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: you may make the complaint under` "s 24(b)(ii)"
#ASSERT `May I make this complaint` `a person the consumer appointed to complain for them` 15 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `ONLYIF`
#ASSERT `May I make this complaint` `a person the consumer appointed to complain for them` 18 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `ONLYIF`
#ASSERT `May I make this complaint` `a parent or guardian of the consumer` 15 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: you may make the complaint under` "s 24(b)(iii)"
#ASSERT `May I make this complaint` `a parent or guardian of the consumer` 16 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `ONLYIF`
#ASSERT `May I make this complaint` `a parent or guardian of the consumer` 16 FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes: you may make the complaint under` "s 24(g)"
#ASSERT `May I make this complaint` `the donee of a power of attorney from the consumer` 80 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: you may make the complaint under` "s 24(d)"
#ASSERT `May I make this complaint` `a substitute decision-maker under the consumer's advance care directive` 80 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: you may make the complaint under` "s 24(da)"
#ASSERT `May I make this complaint` `a person acting for the consumer under another law or a court order` 30 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: you may make the complaint under` "s 24(e)"
#ASSERT `May I make this complaint` `a Member of Parliament` 30 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: you may make the complaint under` "s 24(f)"
#ASSERT `May I make this complaint` `another health or community service provider` 30 FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: you may make the complaint under` "s 24(h)"
#ASSERT `May I make this complaint` `another health or community service provider` 30 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `ONLYIF`
#ASSERT `May I make this complaint` `a person who had an enduring relationship with the consumer` 70 TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes, if you can demonstrate to the Commissioner that you had an enduring relationship with the deceased consumer (s 24(i))`
#ASSERT `May I make this complaint` `a person who had an enduring relationship with the consumer` 70 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `ONLYIF`
#ASSERT `May I make this complaint` `the personal representative of the consumer` 70 TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: you may make the complaint under` "s 24(i)"
#ASSERT `May I make this complaint` `someone else` 50 FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes: you may make the complaint under` "s 24(g)"
#ASSERT `May I make this complaint` `someone else` 50 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `ONLYIF`

§§ `s 25 -- grounds`

`UNREAS` MEANS `yes, if the provider acted unreasonably (for the Commissioner to judge under s 85): this is a ground of complaint under`

#ASSERT `Is this a ground I can complain on` `the provider failed to exercise due skill` `another person` EQUALS `yes: this is a ground of complaint under` "s 25(1)(d)"
#ASSERT `Is this a ground I can complain on` `the service was not necessary or was inappropriate` `another person` EQUALS `yes: this is a ground of complaint under` "s 25(1)(b)"
#ASSERT `Is this a ground I can complain on` `the provider failed to respect the consumer's privacy or dignity` `another person` EQUALS `yes: this is a ground of complaint under` "s 25(1)(f)"
#ASSERT `Is this a ground I can complain on` `the provider acted inconsistently with the Charter` `another person` EQUALS `yes: this is a ground of complaint under` "s 25(1)(k)"
#ASSERT `Is this a ground I can complain on` `the provider did not meet the generally accepted standard of service delivery` `another person` EQUALS `yes: this is a ground of complaint under` "s 25(1)(l)"
#ASSERT `Is this a ground I can complain on` `the provider unreasonably did not provide, or discontinued, a service` `another person` EQUALS `UNREAS` "s 25(1)(a)"
#ASSERT `Is this a ground I can complain on` `the provider unreasonably failed to give the consumer enough information, choice, advice or prognosis` `another person` EQUALS `UNREAS` "s 25(1)(g)"
#ASSERT `Is this a ground I can complain on` `the provider unreasonably denied or restricted access to the consumer's records` `another person` EQUALS `UNREAS` "s 25(1)(h)(i)"
#ASSERT `Is this a ground I can complain on` `the provider unreasonably did not deal properly with the consumer's complaint to it` `another person` EQUALS `UNREAS` "s 25(1)(j)"
#ASSERT `Is this a ground I can complain on` `the provider refused to hand over a copy of, or to alter, the consumer's medical records` `another person` EQUALS `no: nothing in s 25(1) requires a provider to alter, or to hand over a copy of, medical records in its possession (s 25(2)(b)); denying or unreasonably restricting access to them is a ground (s 25(1)(h)(i))`
#ASSERT `Is this a ground I can complain on` `the provider did not act or advise outside its own field of expertise` `another person` EQUALS `no: nothing in s 25(1) requires a provider to act, or to advise, outside the field of expertise of its profession or occupational group (s 25(2)(a))`
#ASSERT `Is this a ground I can complain on` `the provider unreasonably disclosed information about the consumer to a third person` `another person` EQUALS `UNREAS` "s 25(1)(i)"
#ASSERT `Is this a ground I can complain on` `the provider unreasonably disclosed information about the consumer to a third person` `a legal practitioner, in connection with a related legal matter` EQUALS `no: s 25(1)(i) does not apply to a disclosure to a legal practitioner in connection with a related legal matter (s 25(4)(a))`
#ASSERT `Is this a ground I can complain on` `the provider unreasonably disclosed information about the consumer to a third person` `an insurer with an appropriate interest in the information` EQUALS `no: s 25(1)(i) does not apply to a disclosure to an insurer who has an appropriate interest in the information (s 25(4)(b))`
-- the recipient matters only for a disclosure complaint.
#ASSERT `Is this a ground I can complain on` `the provider failed to exercise due skill` `an insurer with an appropriate interest in the information` EQUALS `yes: this is a ground of complaint under` "s 25(1)(d)"
#ASSERT `Is this a ground I can complain on` `something else` `another person` EQUALS `no: a complaint may only be made on the grounds in s 25(1)`

§§ `s 25(5), (6) -- volunteers`

#ASSERT `Who is my complaint about a volunteer against` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the complaint is against the provider who did it: s 25(5) is only about volunteers`
#ASSERT `Who is my complaint about a volunteer against` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the complaint is taken to be against the person or body the volunteer was working for; the volunteer cannot be required to take part in proceedings under the Act (s 25(5))`
#ASSERT `Who is my complaint about a volunteer against` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the complaint is taken to be against the person or body the volunteer was working for; the volunteer cannot be required to take part in proceedings under the Act (s 25(5))`
#ASSERT `Who is my complaint about a volunteer against` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the complaint is taken to be against the person or body the volunteer was working for; the volunteer cannot be required to take part in proceedings under the Act (s 25(5))`
#ASSERT `Who is my complaint about a volunteer against` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the complaint is taken to be against the person or body the volunteer was working for, and the volunteer may also be required to take part and be investigated, as a code of conduct applies to them and the Commissioner is satisfied their conduct poses or posed a risk to public health or safety (s 25(5), (6))`

§§ `s 27 -- the 2-year time limit`

`OUTA` MEANS `out of time: the Commissioner may extend the period only if satisfied that it is appropriate, taking into account whether a proper investigation is still possible, whether the complaint is still amenable to resolution, the public interest and any other relevant matter (s 27(2)(a)); the last day was`
`OUTB` MEANS `out of time, but the Commissioner may extend the period, as the complaint is about a service to a child and you first had notice after May 2004 (s 27(2)(b)); the last day was`
`INTIME` MEANS `in time: the complaint was made within 2 years from the day you first had notice (s 27(1)); the last day was`
`STILL` MEANS `still in time: make the complaint within 2 years from the day you first had notice (s 27(1)); the last day is`

-- Notice 10 March 2024: 2 years from that day ends 10 March 2026 (fork F1).
#ASSERT `By when must I complain` (`the date` 10 3 2024) (`the date` 10 3 2024) TRUE (`the date` 10 3 2026) (`the date` 1 6 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `INTIME` (`the date` 10 3 2026)
#ASSERT `By when must I complain` (`the date` 10 3 2024) (`the date` 10 3 2024) TRUE (`the date` 1 9 2025) (`the date` 1 6 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `INTIME` (`the date` 10 3 2026)
#ASSERT `By when must I complain` (`the date` 10 3 2024) (`the date` 10 3 2024) TRUE (`the date` 11 3 2026) (`the date` 1 6 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `OUTA` (`the date` 10 3 2026)
#ASSERT `By when must I complain` (`the date` 10 3 2024) (`the date` 10 3 2024) TRUE (`the date` 11 3 2026) (`the date` 1 6 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS `OUTB` (`the date` 10 3 2026)
#ASSERT `By when must I complain` (`the date` 10 3 2024) (`the date` 10 3 2024) TRUE (`the date` 11 3 2026) (`the date` 1 6 2026) FALSE TRUE EQUALS `in time as extended: the Commissioner has extended the period in your case (s 27(2))`
-- extension is irrelevant when in time.
#ASSERT `By when must I complain` (`the date` 10 3 2024) (`the date` 10 3 2024) TRUE (`the date` 10 3 2026) (`the date` 1 6 2026) FALSE TRUE EQUALS `INTIME` (`the date` 10 3 2026)
-- Not yet made.
#ASSERT `By when must I complain` (`the date` 10 3 2024) (`the date` 10 3 2024) FALSE `ANY` (`the date` 9 3 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `STILL` (`the date` 10 3 2026)
#ASSERT `By when must I complain` (`the date` 10 3 2024) (`the date` 10 3 2024) FALSE `ANY` (`the date` 10 3 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `STILL` (`the date` 10 3 2026)
#ASSERT `By when must I complain` (`the date` 10 3 2024) (`the date` 10 3 2024) FALSE `ANY` (`the date` 11 3 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `OUTA` (`the date` 10 3 2026)
-- 29 February 2024 plus 2 years: 28 February 2026.
#ASSERT `By when must I complain` (`the date` 29 2 2024) (`the date` 29 2 2024) TRUE (`the date` 28 2 2026) (`the date` 1 6 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `INTIME` (`the date` 28 2 2026)
#ASSERT `By when must I complain` (`the date` 29 2 2024) (`the date` 29 2 2024) TRUE (`the date` 1 3 2026) (`the date` 1 6 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `OUTA` (`the date` 28 2 2026)
-- s 27(3) both ways (fork F4: the earlier day).
#ASSERT `By when must I complain` (`the date` 1 6 2024) (`the date` 1 1 2024) TRUE (`the date` 1 1 2026) (`the date` 1 6 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `INTIME` (`the date` 1 1 2026)
#ASSERT `By when must I complain` (`the date` 1 6 2024) (`the date` 1 1 2024) TRUE (`the date` 2 1 2026) (`the date` 1 6 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `OUTA` (`the date` 1 1 2026)
#ASSERT `By when must I complain` (`the date` 1 1 2024) (`the date` 1 6 2024) TRUE (`the date` 2 1 2026) (`the date` 1 6 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `OUTA` (`the date` 1 1 2026)
-- "after May 2004" (fork F5): 31 May 2004 is not after May; 1 June 2004 is.
#ASSERT `By when must I complain` (`the date` 31 5 2004) (`the date` 31 5 2004) TRUE (`the date` 1 1 2010) (`the date` 1 6 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS `OUTA` (`the date` 31 5 2006)
#ASSERT `By when must I complain` (`the date` 1 6 2004) (`the date` 1 6 2004) TRUE (`the date` 1 1 2010) (`the date` 1 6 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS `OUTB` (`the date` 1 6 2006)

§§ `s 29(5) -- the provider first`

#ASSERT `Must I go to the provider first` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `it may proceed: you took reasonable steps to resolve the matter with the provider first (s 29(5))`
#ASSERT `Must I go to the provider first` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `it may proceed: you took reasonable steps to resolve the matter with the provider first (s 29(5))`
#ASSERT `Must I go to the provider first` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `it may proceed: you had good reason for not first trying to resolve the matter with the provider (s 29(5))`
#ASSERT `Must I go to the provider first` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `it should not proceed, if it appears to the Commissioner that you failed, without good reason, to take reasonable steps to resolve the matter with the provider before complaining (s 29(5))`

§§ `s 28A -- the Ombudsman`

#ASSERT `Will my child protection complaint go to the Ombudsman` `a notification of a suspicion that a child may be at risk` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `it goes to the Ombudsman: it is a prescribed child protection complaint, which the Commissioner must refer to the Ombudsman to be dealt with under the Ombudsman Act 1972 (s 28A(1), (8))`
#ASSERT `Will my child protection complaint go to the Ombudsman` `a service to or for a child under the guardianship or in the custody of the Minister or another person under the Children and Young People (Safety) Act 2016` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `it goes to the Ombudsman: it is a prescribed child protection complaint, which the Commissioner must refer to the Ombudsman to be dealt with under the Ombudsman Act 1972 (s 28A(1), (8))`
#ASSERT `Will my child protection complaint go to the Ombudsman` `a service to or for a child who may be or has been at risk` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the Commissioner deals with it: it is a prescribed child protection complaint, but in a class the administrative arrangement with the Ombudsman leaves with the Commissioner (s 28A(2))`
#ASSERT `Will my child protection complaint go to the Ombudsman` `a service to or for a child who may be or has been at risk` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: it is not a prescribed child protection complaint (s 28A(8), a "means" definition), so s 28A does not send it to the Ombudsman`
#ASSERT `Will my child protection complaint go to the Ombudsman` `none of these` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: it is not a prescribed child protection complaint (s 28A(8), a "means" definition), so s 28A does not send it to the Ombudsman`

§§ `ss 29(3), 57 -- who deals with it`

#ASSERT `Who will deal with my complaint` `a nationally registered health practitioner` EQUALS `the matter proceeds under Part 8 of the Health Practitioner Regulation National Law (South Australia), not under s 57(1) to (4) (s 57(5))`
#ASSERT `Who will deal with my complaint` `another registered service provider` EQUALS `the Commissioner should consult the registration authority about managing it, and it may be referred to that authority if both agree (s 57(1) to (4)); the authority may also take interim measures on the provider's right to practise (s 65)`
#ASSERT `Who will deal with my complaint` `an approved provider under the Aged Care Act 1997 of the Commonwealth` EQUALS `the Commissioner must consult the Commonwealth aged care complaints resolution bodies, and may refer it to another authority under that Act (s 29(3))`
#ASSERT `Who will deal with my complaint` `a provider that is not registered` EQUALS `the Commissioner assesses it and may conciliate, investigate, refer or take no further action (s 29(2))`

§§ `s 28 -- the Commissioner's requirement`

-- Requirement 1 October 2026, period to 15 October 2026.
#ASSERT `Was I in time with the Commissioner's request` (`the date` 1 10 2026) (`the date` 15 10 2026) TRUE (`the date` 15 10 2026) (`the date` 1 11 2026) FALSE EQUALS `in time: you met the requirement within the period specified or extended (s 28(2), (3)); the last day was` (`the date` 15 10 2026)
#ASSERT `Was I in time with the Commissioner's request` (`the date` 1 10 2026) (`the date` 15 10 2026) TRUE (`the date` 16 10 2026) (`the date` 1 11 2026) TRUE EQUALS `late, but with good reason: the Commissioner may act under s 33(1)(h) only on a failure without good reason; the Commissioner may still extend the period after it has expired (s 28(3)); the last day was` (`the date` 15 10 2026)
#ASSERT `Was I in time with the Commissioner's request` (`the date` 1 10 2026) (`the date` 15 10 2026) TRUE (`the date` 16 10 2026) (`the date` 1 11 2026) FALSE EQUALS `late: if you failed without good reason, the Commissioner may determine to take no further action on, or to suspend action on, your complaint (s 33(1)(h)), and may still extend the period after it has expired (s 28(3)); the last day was` (`the date` 15 10 2026)
#ASSERT `Was I in time with the Commissioner's request` (`the date` 1 10 2026) (`the date` 15 10 2026) FALSE `ANY` (`the date` 15 10 2026) FALSE EQUALS `still in time: meet the requirement by the last day of the period specified or extended (s 28(2), (3)), which is` (`the date` 15 10 2026)
#ASSERT `Was I in time with the Commissioner's request` (`the date` 1 10 2026) (`the date` 15 10 2026) FALSE `ANY` (`the date` 16 10 2026) FALSE EQUALS `late: if you failed without good reason, the Commissioner may determine to take no further action on, or to suspend action on, your complaint (s 33(1)(h)), and may still extend the period after it has expired (s 28(3)); the last day was` (`the date` 15 10 2026)

§§ `s 29(1) -- assessment within 45 days`

-- Received 1 March 2026: 30 days to 31 March, 15 more to 15 April 2026 (45).
#ASSERT `By when must the Commissioner decide on my complaint` (`the date` 1 3 2026) 0 TRUE (`the date` 15 4 2026) (`the date` 1 6 2026) EQUALS `in time: done on or before the last day, which was` (`the date` 15 4 2026)
#ASSERT `By when must the Commissioner decide on my complaint` (`the date` 1 3 2026) 0 TRUE (`the date` 16 4 2026) (`the date` 1 6 2026) EQUALS `late: done after the last day, which was` (`the date` 15 4 2026)
-- 10 days of allowed delay: 55 days, 25 April 2026.
#ASSERT `By when must the Commissioner decide on my complaint` (`the date` 1 3 2026) 10 TRUE (`the date` 16 4 2026) (`the date` 1 6 2026) EQUALS `in time: done on or before the last day, which was` (`the date` 25 4 2026)
#ASSERT `By when must the Commissioner decide on my complaint` (`the date` 1 3 2026) 10 FALSE `ANY` (`the date` 20 4 2026) EQUALS `not yet done, and still in time: the last day is` (`the date` 25 4 2026)
#ASSERT `By when must the Commissioner decide on my complaint` (`the date` 1 3 2026) 10 FALSE `ANY` (`the date` 26 4 2026) EQUALS `not yet done, and the last day has passed: it was` (`the date` 25 4 2026)
-- Received 20 December 2026: 11 days to 31 December, 31 more to 31 January (42), 3 more to 3 February 2027 (45).
#ASSERT `By when must the Commissioner decide on my complaint` (`the date` 20 12 2026) 0 FALSE `ANY` (`the date` 3 2 2027) EQUALS `not yet done, and still in time: the last day is` (`the date` 3 2 2027)

§§ `s 29(6) -- written notice within 14 days`

#ASSERT `By when must I be told the decision on my complaint` (`the date` 15 4 2026) TRUE (`the date` 29 4 2026) (`the date` 1 6 2026) EQUALS `in time: done on or before the last day, which was` (`the date` 29 4 2026)
#ASSERT `By when must I be told the decision on my complaint` (`the date` 15 4 2026) TRUE (`the date` 30 4 2026) (`the date` 1 6 2026) EQUALS `late: done after the last day, which was` (`the date` 29 4 2026)
#ASSERT `By when must I be told the decision on my complaint` (`the date` 15 4 2026) FALSE `ANY` (`the date` 1 5 2026) EQUALS `not yet done, and the last day has passed: it was` (`the date` 29 4 2026)
