§§ `s 33 -- stopping or suspending`

`MAYSTOP` MEANS `the Commissioner may determine to take no further action, or to suspend action, with written notice to you (s 33(1), (4)), on the ground in`
`SUSPEND` MEANS `the Commissioner must suspend action: court proceedings or a coroner's inquest on the subject matter have been commenced (s 33(3)); you must be given written notice (s 33(4)), and action may be recommenced for any reasonable cause (s 33(5))`

#ASSERT `Can the Commissioner stop dealing with my complaint` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `none of the s 33(1) grounds` EQUALS `the Commissioner must take no further action: all issues arising out of the subject matter have been adjudicated (s 33(2)); you must be given written notice (s 33(4))`
#ASSERT `Can the Commissioner stop dealing with my complaint` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `none of the s 33(1) grounds` EQUALS `SUSPEND`
#ASSERT `Can the Commissioner stop dealing with my complaint` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `none of the s 33(1) grounds` EQUALS `SUSPEND`
#ASSERT `Can the Commissioner stop dealing with my complaint` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE `none of the s 33(1) grounds` EQUALS `MAYSTOP` "s 33(1)(d)"
#ASSERT `Can the Commissioner stop dealing with my complaint` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `the matter should be determined by legal proceedings` EQUALS `MAYSTOP` "s 33(1)(c)"
#ASSERT `Can the Commissioner stop dealing with my complaint` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `I relied on a ground I should have disclosed earlier` EQUALS `MAYSTOP` "s 33(1)(f), with s 26(2)"
#ASSERT `Can the Commissioner stop dealing with my complaint` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `the complaint has been resolved or abandoned` EQUALS `MAYSTOP` "s 33(1)(j)"
#ASSERT `Can the Commissioner stop dealing with my complaint` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `none of the s 33(1) grounds` EQUALS `only for some other reasonable cause that justifies discontinuing or suspending (s 33(1)(k)): none of the other grounds in s 33 is present`

§§ `s 34 -- withdrawal`

#ASSERT `What happens if I withdraw my complaint` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `not withdrawn: a complaint is withdrawn by written notice to the Commissioner, which you may give at any time (s 34(1))`
#ASSERT `What happens if I withdraw my complaint` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `withdrawn: any investigation of it ceases (s 34(2)(a))`
#ASSERT `What happens if I withdraw my complaint` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `withdrawn, but the investigation of the significant issue or question it raised may go on (ss 34(2)(a), 43(1)(c), (2)(c))`
#ASSERT `What happens if I withdraw my complaint` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `withdrawn: any investigation of it ceases, but the person or body it was referred to may still act on the matters it raised (s 34(2)(a), (3))`
#ASSERT `What happens if I withdraw my complaint` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `withdrawn, but the investigation of the significant issue or question may go on, and the person or body it was referred to may still act on the matters it raised (ss 34(2)(a), (3), 43(1)(c))`

§§ `ss 29(4), 30, 39 -- conciliation`

`NOCONC` MEANS `no: the Commissioner must not refer the complaint to a conciliator, and informal mediation should not occur, because it appears to indicate a significant issue of public safety, interest or importance or a significant question as to a provider's practice (ss 29(4), 30(8)); a conciliation or mediation already begun must be brought to an end (ss 30(11)(a), 39(3))`

#ASSERT `Can my complaint go to conciliation` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `it may: the Commissioner may refer the complaint to a conciliator (s 29(2)(a)) or assist the parties through informal mediation (s 30(7)); neither is required, and either must end at your request (ss 30(11)(b), 39(4))`
#ASSERT `Can my complaint go to conciliation` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `NOCONC`
#ASSERT `Can my complaint go to conciliation` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `NOCONC`

§§ `s 37 -- help at conciliation`

#ASSERT `Can someone help me at conciliation` `assisting me` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: a party to a conciliation may be assisted by another person (s 37(1))`
#ASSERT `Can someone help me at conciliation` `assisting me` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: the conciliator has directed that this person not be allowed to act in the matter (s 37(2))`
#ASSERT `Can someone help me at conciliation` `representing me` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes: you may be represented, as the Commissioner is satisfied that representation is likely to assist substantially in resolving the complaint (s 37(3))`
#ASSERT `Can someone help me at conciliation` `representing me` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: a party may not be represented except where the Commissioner is satisfied that representation is likely to assist substantially in resolving the complaint (s 37(3))`
-- fork F7: the s 37(2) direction is read as reaching assistance only.
#ASSERT `Can someone help me at conciliation` `representing me` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: you may be represented, as the Commissioner is satisfied that representation is likely to assist substantially in resolving the complaint (s 37(3))`

§§ `ss 30(10), 40(1), 45(6) -- using what was said`

#ASSERT `Can what was said in conciliation be used in court` `conciliation by a conciliator` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: anything said or done in it is not to be disclosed in any other proceedings, under any Act or law, without the parties' consent` "s 40(1)"
#ASSERT `Can what was said in conciliation be used in court` `conciliation by a conciliator` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the bar does not cover it: it reveals a significant issue of public safety, interest or importance` "s 40(1)"
#ASSERT `Can what was said in conciliation be used in court` `informal mediation during a preliminary inquiry` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes, by consent: the parties have all consented to its disclosure` "s 30(10)"
#ASSERT `Can what was said in conciliation be used in court` `conciliation attempted during an investigation` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: anything said or done in it is not to be disclosed in any other proceedings, under any Act or law, without the parties' consent` "s 45(6)"

§§ `s 42 -- the binding agreement`

-- Verbal agreement 1 September 2026: 14 days after is 15 September 2026.
#ASSERT `Is my conciliation agreement binding` TRUE (`the date` 1 9 2026) TRUE (`the date` 15 9 2026) (`the date` 1 10 2026) EQUALS `it can be binding: it was entered into in writing within 14 days after the verbal agreement (s 42(1), (2)); the last day was` (`the date` 15 9 2026)
#ASSERT `Is my conciliation agreement binding` TRUE (`the date` 1 9 2026) TRUE (`the date` 16 9 2026) (`the date` 1 10 2026) EQUALS `not binding: it was not entered into in writing within 14 days after the verbal agreement (s 42(2)); the last day was` (`the date` 15 9 2026)
#ASSERT `Is my conciliation agreement binding` TRUE (`the date` 1 9 2026) FALSE `ANY` (`the date` 10 9 2026) EQUALS `not binding yet: to be binding it must be entered into in writing within 14 days after the verbal agreement (s 42(2)); the last day is` (`the date` 15 9 2026)
#ASSERT `Is my conciliation agreement binding` TRUE (`the date` 1 9 2026) FALSE `ANY` (`the date` 16 9 2026) EQUALS `not binding: it was not entered into in writing within 14 days after the verbal agreement (s 42(2)); the last day was` (`the date` 15 9 2026)
#ASSERT `Is my conciliation agreement binding` FALSE (`the date` 1 9 2026) FALSE `ANY` (`the date` 16 9 2026) EQUALS `s 42 does not affect it: an agreement reached outside the conciliation process is as effective as it otherwise would be (s 42(3))`

§§ `ss 54, 55, 56D -- copies`

#ASSERT `Will I get a copy of the outcome` `a report of the investigation's findings and conclusions` TRUE EQUALS `not as of right: the Commissioner may give copies of an investigation report to such persons as the Commissioner thinks fit (s 54(2))`
#ASSERT `Will I get a copy of the outcome` `a notice of recommended action to the provider` TRUE EQUALS `you are to be advised that the notice was given to the provider, if the Commissioner gives one (s 55(1)(b)); the provider has at least 28 days to respond (s 55(5))`
#ASSERT `Will I get a copy of the outcome` `a report the Commissioner publishes after a notice of recommended action` FALSE EQUALS `yes: the Commissioner must give a copy of the report to any complainant who was a party to the proceedings (s 55(10))`
#ASSERT `Will I get a copy of the outcome` `a statement of action taken against the provider under s 56C` TRUE EQUALS `yes, if the action relates to your complaint: the Commissioner must give you a copy of the statement (s 56D(2)(a))`
#ASSERT `Will I get a copy of the outcome` `a statement of action taken against the provider under s 56C` FALSE EQUALS `no: the Commissioner must give a copy of a s 56D statement to the complainant only where the action relates to a complaint (s 56D(2)(a))`

§§ `ss 56B, 56C, 56F, reg 8 -- orders against the provider`

`FINAL` MEANS `yes: the Commissioner may make an order prohibiting the provider from providing health services (or imposing conditions) for a specified period or indefinitely, and publish a public statement (s 56C(2)); contravening the order carries a maximum penalty of $10 000 or 2 years' imprisonment or both (s 56C(4)); if it relates to your complaint you get a copy of the statement of reasons (s 56D(2)(a))`
`INTERIM` MEANS `yes: the Commissioner may make an interim order prohibiting the provider from providing health services (or imposing conditions) for 12 weeks or a shorter period, and publish a public statement (s 56B(2)); contravening the order carries a maximum penalty of $10 000 or 2 years' imprisonment or both (s 56B(5))`
`NOREACH` MEANS `ss 56B and 56C do not reach this: neither section's conditions are all met on these facts`

#ASSERT `Can the provider be stopped from practising` TRUE `an investigation has been carried out` `a breach of the prescribed code of conduct that applies to them` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: action under Division 5 may not be taken on conduct within Part 7 (the registration authorities' part) (s 56F(2))`
#ASSERT `Can the provider be stopped from practising` FALSE `an investigation has been carried out` `a breach of the prescribed code of conduct that applies to them` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `FINAL`
#ASSERT `Can the provider be stopped from practising` FALSE `an investigation has been carried out` `an offence against Part 3 of the Criminal Law Consolidation Act 1935` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `FINAL`
#ASSERT `Can the provider be stopped from practising` FALSE `an investigation has been commenced` `an offence against the Australian Consumer Law (SA)` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `INTERIM`
-- 56C needs the investigation carried out; with it only commenced, 56C's conditions fail.
#ASSERT `Can the provider be stopped from practising` FALSE `an investigation has been commenced` `an offence against the South Australian Public Health Act 2011` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `NOREACH`
-- carried out, but no unacceptable risk: 56B is still open on belief and necessity.
#ASSERT `Can the provider be stopped from practising` FALSE `an investigation has been carried out` `an offence against Part 7 Division 10 of the Health Practitioner Regulation National Law (South Australia)` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `INTERIM`
#ASSERT `Can the provider be stopped from practising` FALSE `an investigation has been carried out` `another offence` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `NOREACH`
#ASSERT `Can the provider be stopped from practising` FALSE `no investigation` `a breach of the prescribed code of conduct that applies to them` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `NOREACH`

§§ `s 74 -- identity`

#ASSERT `Can my identity be kept from the provider` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes, the Commissioner may withhold it: the Commissioner believes on reasonable grounds that disclosure would put a person's health or safety at risk, lower the standard of service a person receives, or prejudice the fair assessment of the complaint (s 74(a))`
#ASSERT `Can my identity be kept from the provider` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes, the Commissioner may withhold it: the complaint raises a significant public issue or question as to a provider's practice, and non-disclosure is in the public interest (s 74(b))`
#ASSERT `Can my identity be kept from the provider` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `s 74 does not reach this: the Commissioner may withhold your identity from the provider only in the circumstances it states`
#ASSERT `Can my identity be kept from the provider` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `s 74 does not reach this: the Commissioner may withhold your identity from the provider only in the circumstances it states`

§§ `ss 78, 79 -- reprisals`

#ASSERT `Is it an offence to punish me for complaining` `threats or intimidation to stop me complaining, make me withdraw, not co-operate, withhold information, or give false information` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes: it is an offence to persuade or try to persuade you by threat or intimidation in this way; maximum penalty $10 000 (s 78)`
#ASSERT `Is it an offence to punish me for complaining` `unfavourable treatment because I complained, co-operated or gave information, or was thought about to` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: it is an offence to treat you unfavourably on that ground, and it is enough that it was a significant factor; maximum penalty $10 000 (s 79(1), (2))`
#ASSERT `Is it an offence to punish me for complaining` `unfavourable treatment because I complained, co-operated or gave information, or was thought about to` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: unfavourable treatment on the ground that you made a false allegation, or did not act in good faith, does not contravene s 79(1) (s 79(3))`
#ASSERT `Is it an offence to punish me for complaining` `unfavourable treatment because I complained, co-operated or gave information, or was thought about to` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: s 79(1) is about treatment on the ground of the complaint, co-operation or information, and that was not even a significant factor (s 79(1), (2))`
#ASSERT `Is it an offence to punish me for complaining` `something else` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `ss 78 and 79 do not make this an offence`

§§ `s 83 -- civil liability`

#ASSERT `Can I be sued for complaining` TRUE EQUALS `no: you are not liable for loss, damage or injury of any kind that another person suffers as a result of your complaint, or of statements, information or documents you gave under the Act, done in good faith (s 83(1)(a), (b))`
#ASSERT `Can I be sued for complaining` FALSE EQUALS `s 83 gives no protection on these facts: it covers only what is done in good faith`
